  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I had a hard time installing Fedora Repository 3.1 on Unix thanks to the need for a writable FEDORA_HOME. Typically Unix software is installed by an admin, and users given limited privileges to the few files and directories they absolutely need to write to.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Obviously there needs to be an area where datastreams are kept, but requiring all of FEDORA_HOME (children directories included) to be writable seems somewhat excessive. FEDORA_HOME contains mostly code and configuration files, which don't need to (and in fact, shouldn't) be written to by Fedora. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Through trial and error, I got away with allowing only the following directories to be writable:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "FEDORA_HOME/data",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "FEDORA_HOME/server/status",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "FEDORA_HOME/server/logs",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "FEDORA_HOME/server/management",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "FEDORA_HOME/server/fedora-internal-use",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "FEDORA_HOME/server/fedora-internal-use/fedora-internal-use-backend-service-policies",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "I think it would be quite helpful to document which specific directories need to be writable, and maybe consolidate them into one place. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
